I take my big blue kurta, white shirt, and red scarf.
I go to the billing counter.
That young salesman is there.
I give him these three pieces of clothing.
I like this big blue kurta a lot.
The white shirt is very good.
And this red scarf is beautiful.
The salesman looks at the clothes' prices.
I ask, "Brother, how many rupees is the total?"
He says, "Madam, the total is one thousand two hundred rupees."
I give him one thousand two hundred rupees.
I say, "Brother, I want a big bag."
He gives me a big bag.
He puts the bill in the bag.
I happily pack my new clothes into the bag.
These new cotton clothes are very light.
In the summer, I always wear such cotton clothes.
I take the bag and come out of the shop.
